From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:40:00 -0300
Subject: Wayland EGL: a window drawn as a pair may say its pair is 3D content

An engine that draws a window once per eye (the edition's Qt Quick)
gets the surface's two views through _q_stereo_views, and the EGL
window marks that pair as the desktop's own depth: a 2D picture whose
elements show depth. A 3D program whose two views are two cameras (a
stereo surface format, drawn per eye by Qt Quick 3D) is content, not
depth, and the EGL implementation already declares it as full side by
side. Such a window says so with the dynamic property
_q_stereo_content, and gets no desktop-depth mark; without the
property nothing changes.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
Index: src/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
===================================================================
--- src.orig/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
+++ src/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,13 @@ QT_BEGIN_NAMESPACE
 
 namespace QtWaylandClient {
 
+// A window drawn as a pair by its engine whose two views are 3D content (two cameras), not a 2D
+// picture with depth: it says so with _q_stereo_content, and gets no desktop-depth mark.
+bool QWaylandEglWindow::contentPair() const
+{
+    return window()->property("_q_stereo_content").toBool();
+}
+
 QWaylandEglWindow::QWaylandEglWindow(QWindow *window, QWaylandDisplay *display)
     : QWaylandWindow(window, display)
     , m_clientBufferIntegration(static_cast<QWaylandEglClientBufferIntegration *>(mDisplay->clientBufferIntegration()))
@@ -131,8 +138,9 @@ void QWaylandEglWindow::updateSurface(bo
             setFormat(eglFormat);
 
             // The EGL implementation declares the two views as a full side-by-side pair; an engine's
-            // pair is marked, with the same first commit, as the desktop's own depth.
-            QWaylandStereoDepth::setDesktopDepth(this, pair);
+            // pair is marked, with the same first commit, as the desktop's own depth, unless the window
+            // says its pair is 3D content (_q_stereo_content: two cameras, as a quad-buffer program's).
+            QWaylandStereoDepth::setDesktopDepth(this, pair && !contentPair());
 
             EGLSurface eglSurface = eglCreateWindowSurface(m_clientBufferIntegration->eglDisplay(), eglConfig, (EGLNativeWindowType) eglWindow, stereo ? surfaceAttribs : nullptr);
             if (Q_UNLIKELY(eglSurface == EGL_NO_SURFACE)) {
@@ -219,8 +227,9 @@ void QWaylandEglWindow::beginFrameViews(
         return;
 
     if (m_clientBufferIntegration->supportsStereo(fmt)) {
-        // A stereo window has two views either way: only the mark changes.
-        QWaylandStereoDepth::setDesktopDepth(this, pair);
+        // A stereo window has two views either way: only the mark changes, and a window whose pair is
+        // 3D content carries none.
+        QWaylandStereoDepth::setDesktopDepth(this, pair && !contentPair());
         m_pairSurface = pair;
         return;
     }
Index: src/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow_p.h
===================================================================
--- src.orig/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow_p.h
+++ src/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow_p.h
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ public:
     // of a frame, a surface that should now have a different number of views is destroyed, so it
     // is created again with them.
     void beginFrameViews();
+    bool contentPair() const;
 
 protected:
     bool eventFilter(QObject *watched, QEvent *event) override;
